From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sean Dolbec <sdolbec1@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 21:00:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132: Describe the NVMe controller and
 NVMMU windows

This tree's T8132 ANS2 support (apple_nvme_t8132_hw) maps the NVMMU from
its own "nvmmu" resource and fails to probe without it. The T8132 ANS
has two windows: the ADT's /arm-io/ans reg[9] is the NVMe controller and
reg[3] is the NVMMU, the split m1n1 uses for every chip with
nvme-secure-bar. On T8132 they are at 0x4c5cc0000 and 0x485cc0000, the
same layout as T8140 (0x3cdcc0000 and 0x38dcc0000).

Add the 0x60000 NVMMU window, which holds the TCB registers at
+0x28100..+0x28120. Keep the controller window at 0x60000 rather than
the 0x28000 the linear queue registers need: GravityLinux's driver
reaches the NVMMU registers through this alias at the same offsets, and
our J773g runs from its SSD that way today. Keeping the window lets one
device tree boot both kernels, which matters while J773g owners move
between them and as a fallback while this tree is tested.

The window split follows KB2UKA's reading of the J713 ADT
(Kb2uka/Omarchy-M4-Native, "fix(dts): t8132: split M4 NVMe and NVMMU
windows"). This layout has not been booted with this tree's driver yet.

Signed-off-by: Sean Dolbec <sdolbec1@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
index c147568e73..d7f643d495 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
@@ -507,9 +507,15 @@
 
 		nvme: nvme@4c5cc0000 {
 			compatible = "apple,t8132-nvme-ans2";
+			/*
+			 * ADT reg[9] is the controller window and reg[3] the
+			 * NVMMU. The controller window also aliases the NVMMU
+			 * registers, which older kernels use.
+			 */
 			reg = <0x4 0xc5cc0000 0x0 0x60000>,
-			      <0x4 0x81600000 0x0 0x4000>;
-			reg-names = "nvme", "ans";
+			      <0x4 0x81600000 0x0 0x4000>,
+			      <0x4 0x85cc0000 0x0 0x60000>;
+			reg-names = "nvme", "ans", "nvmmu";
 
 			interrupt-parent = <&aic>;
 			interrupts = <AIC_IRQ 1018 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
